WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.750 --> 00:00:06.090
After the first two episodes of WandaVision
dropped on Disney+, fans of the Marvel Cinematic

00:00:06.090 --> 00:00:12.160
Universe immediately set to work, picking
apart every little detail of the classic TV-inspired

00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:13.700
pseudo-sitcom.

00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:19.160
There are lots of people, places, and even
objects that potentially hint at how WandaVision

00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:22.680
could change Marvel's TV universe going forward.

00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:25.080
Take Westview community leader Dottie.

00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:29.850
Dottie, like many of the residents of Westview,
is already beginning to see through the cracks

00:00:29.850 --> 00:00:31.619
in WandaVision's world.

00:00:31.619 --> 00:00:36.280
As she and Wanda clean up after a town planning
event, she makes it clear that she has "heard

00:00:36.280 --> 00:00:40.920
things" about Wanda and Vision and, moreover,
doesn't trust them.

00:00:40.920 --> 00:00:45.810
More than that, when a mysterious voice calling
Wanda's name is heard coming through the static

00:00:45.810 --> 00:00:50.200
of a nearby radio, both Wanda and Dottie are
able to hear it.

00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:54.920
It's obvious that there's more to Westview
and Dottie than meets the eye, and the actor

00:00:54.920 --> 00:00:58.960
who plays her likely seems more than a bit
familiar.

00:00:58.960 --> 00:01:06.210
"Nothing like what you two just did has ever
happened in the history of our talent show!"

00:01:06.210 --> 00:01:11.250
Her name is Emma Caulfield Ford, and this
is far from her first foray into the world

00:01:11.250 --> 00:01:13.640
of science fiction and fantasy.

00:01:13.640 --> 00:01:18.840
Perhaps you've seen her in Fear the Walking
Dead, Supergirl, Once Upon a Time, or another

00:01:18.840 --> 00:01:22.060
of her dozens of TV appearances over the years.

00:01:22.060 --> 00:01:26.320
But, chances are, you know her from Buffy
the Vampire Slayer.

00:01:26.320 --> 00:01:32.290
In Season 3 of Buffy, Cordelia Chase wishes
that Buffy Summers had never come to Sunnydale,

00:01:32.290 --> 00:01:37.160
thus creating an alternate universe ruled
by The Master and overrun by his creatures

00:01:37.160 --> 00:01:41.190
of the night, in one of the most iconic episodes
of the show.

00:01:41.190 --> 00:01:45.780
The "scary, veiny, good fairy" who made Cordy's
wish come true?

00:01:45.780 --> 00:01:51.830
Why, that would be none other than Emma Caulfield
Ford, known at the time as just "Emma Caulfield,"

00:01:51.830 --> 00:01:54.240
as the vengeance demon Anya.

00:01:54.240 --> 00:01:58.829
It wouldn't be until the fourth season of
Buffy that Anya would be slotted in as a series

00:01:58.829 --> 00:02:03.149
regular, but it didn't take long before fans
realized the character would become far more

00:02:03.149 --> 00:02:08.009
than Cordelia's replacement after she absconded
to Los Angeles with Angel.

00:02:08.009 --> 00:02:13.620
Anya was a fresh, snarky take on the "inhuman
being must learn to be human" trope.

00:02:13.620 --> 00:02:18.840
After centuries of helping scorned women take
extreme revenge on the men who spurned them,

00:02:18.840 --> 00:02:23.680
Anya becomes friends with Buffy and the gang
while also falling in love with Xander Harris.

00:02:23.680 --> 00:02:29.470
The romance between Anya and Xander is a huge
part of the Buffy story, and very nearly leads

00:02:29.470 --> 00:02:30.720
to marriage.

00:02:30.720 --> 00:02:35.720
Of course, it wouldn't be Buffy if true love
didn't lead to misery, so we get to see Anya

00:02:35.720 --> 00:02:40.910
cope with being a vengeance demon all over
again, making her one of the most complex

00:02:40.910 --> 00:02:44.000
characters in Buffy's seven-season history.

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:48.820
The same year that Buffy the Vampire Slayer
concluded it's seven-season run, Emma Caulfield

00:02:48.820 --> 00:02:53.540
Ford was already starring in a horror movie
with a concept that actually feels like it

00:02:53.540 --> 00:02:57.740
could've come straight out of an episode of
Buffy — Darkness Falls.

00:02:57.740 --> 00:03:03.040
Darkness Falls is both the name of the 2003
film and the town in which the story is set,

00:03:03.040 --> 00:03:07.720
raising the question — who would choose
to live in a town named Darkness Falls?

00:03:07.720 --> 00:03:12.940
The answer, as you might have guessed, is
Emma Caulfield Ford playing Caitlin Greene.

00:03:12.940 --> 00:03:18.630
In A Nightmare on Elm Street, Wes Craven found
success redefining the Sandman as a knife-fingered

00:03:18.630 --> 00:03:22.690
monster who kills you in your dreams named
Freddy Krueger.

00:03:22.690 --> 00:03:27.989
Darkness Falls performs a similar trick, but
this time it's the Tooth Fairy getting a murderous

00:03:27.989 --> 00:03:28.989
makeover.

00:03:28.989 --> 00:03:33.080
Just like the parents from Elm Street killed
Krueger, the parents of Darkness Falls kill

00:03:33.080 --> 00:03:38.769
Matilda Dixon, a.k.a. the Tooth Fairy; the
difference is that Matilda Dixon was innocent

00:03:38.769 --> 00:03:40.879
of the crimes she was accused of.

00:03:40.879 --> 00:03:46.610
The result is the same: The Tooth Fairy becomes
a vengeful spirit and returns to do some killing.

00:03:46.610 --> 00:03:51.630
Considering Caulfield Ford just wrapped playing
a vengeance demon on Buffy, she naturally

00:03:51.630 --> 00:03:55.049
was the perfect person to fight an evil Tooth
Fairy.

00:03:55.049 --> 00:04:00.110
Two years before Black Mirror existed in any
form, Emma Caulfield Ford starred as Oona

00:04:00.110 --> 00:04:05.720
O'Leary in 2009's TiMER — a movie with a
very similar premise to the Black Mirror episode

00:04:05.720 --> 00:04:07.220
"Hang the DJ."

00:04:07.220 --> 00:04:12.150
In the future, most people accept who their
"soulmate" will be via a high-tech dating

00:04:12.150 --> 00:04:13.150
app.

00:04:13.150 --> 00:04:17.310
The app in TiMER is a device installed in
the wrist that counts down to when a person

00:04:17.310 --> 00:04:21.650
will meet their soulmate, but Oona's clock
is not counting down.

00:04:21.650 --> 00:04:23.210
Does she have no soulmate?

00:04:23.210 --> 00:04:24.840
Is her soulmate dead?

00:04:24.840 --> 00:04:28.990
Or has her soulmate simply not gotten their
own device installed?

00:04:28.990 --> 00:04:33.810
TiMER is a classic science fiction exploration
of free will versus destiny set through the

00:04:33.810 --> 00:04:35.870
lens of a romantic comedy.

00:04:35.870 --> 00:04:40.620
Plus, there are two interesting things about
TiMER as it pertains to WandaVision.

00:04:40.620 --> 00:04:44.910
The first is that there seems to be a question
of whether or not the residents of Westview

00:04:44.910 --> 00:04:47.910
are there of their own free will or not.

00:04:47.910 --> 00:04:53.090
Even more interesting, however, is that Jac
Schaeffer, who wrote and directed TiMER, is

00:04:53.090 --> 00:04:55.389
also the showrunner for WandaVision.

00:04:55.389 --> 00:05:00.301
So if there's any role from Caulfield Ford's
past that's relevant to WandaVision, it's

00:05:00.301 --> 00:05:02.740
definitely Oona from TiMER.

00:05:02.740 --> 00:05:05.060
"Now you can clap."

00:05:05.060 --> 00:05:07.979
"And stop."

